Subject: [PATCH] dwc2: recover root-hub activation seeing stale device mode
Upstream-Status: Pending

_dwc2_hcd_start() ("Starts the HCD when switching to Host mode") opens with

	if (dwc2_is_device_mode(hsotg)) {
		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&hsotg->lock, flags);
		return 0;	/* why 0 ?? */
	}

- an unexplained, entirely silent early return that skips
dwc2_hcd_reinit(), dwc2_vbus_supply_init() and, critically,
usb_hcd_resume_root_hub(). The root hub is never activated and the host
controller's port connect/enable/overcurrent interrupts never get enabled,
with nothing in dmesg to explain why.

hsotg->wq_otg is an ordered workqueue (alloc_ordered_workqueue() in
dwc2_hcd_init()), so this function - queued as hsotg->start_work by
dwc2_hcd_start() - cannot run concurrently with
dwc2_conn_id_status_change(): it only runs after the A-Device/host branch
that queued it has returned, i.e. after
dwc2_core_init()->dwc2_core_reset() has already confirmed host mode. So
dwc2_is_device_mode() should not be true here. The most plausible way it
becomes true anyway is a second Connector ID Status Change interrupt
queuing another dwc2_conn_id_status_change() job on the same ordered queue
ahead of start_work, which - if it takes the B-Device branch - flips the
mode back before start_work gets its turn.

Captured dmesg from a real role switch on this hardware (Carlinkit Mini
Ultra, Ingenic X1600, Toyota Proace Verso NAC Wave 2) shows two racing
dwc2_wait_for_mode(host) calls around one force_mode(host) request (see
patch 0039) and zero port interrupt activity for the entire accessory-probe
window afterwards, consistent with the root hub never being activated.

Replace the silent return with a loud warning naming the state, a bounded
retry (up to 200ms, the worst-case mode-switch time measured here), and
either confirmation of recovery or an error making the permanent failure
visible instead of silent.

Whether this is the actual failure mode on this hardware is not yet
established - patch 0022's HPRT0 instrumentation is what settles it. The
recovery is worth having either way: the silent return is a real hole.

---
 drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd.c |  46 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 45 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd.c
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/dma-mapping.h>
 #include <linux/delay.h>
+#include <linux/jiffies.h>
 #include <linux/io.h>
 #include <linux/slab.h>
 #include <linux/usb.h>
@@ -4319,8 +4320,51 @@
 	set_bit(HCD_FLAG_HW_ACCESSIBLE, &hcd->flags);
 
 	if (dwc2_is_device_mode(hsotg)) {
+		unsigned long timeout;
+
 		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&hsotg->lock, flags);
-		return 0;	/* why 0 ?? */
+
+		/*
+		 * Normally the mode is already host here: this function only
+		 * runs (queued as hsotg->start_work on the ordered
+		 * hsotg->wq_otg workqueue) after dwc2_conn_id_status_change()'s
+		 * A-Device branch has already confirmed host mode. Seeing
+		 * device mode means something flipped it back in between - for
+		 * example a second Connector ID Status Change interrupt queuing
+		 * another dwc2_conn_id_status_change() job ahead of this one on
+		 * the same ordered workqueue.
+		 *
+		 * This used to silently return 0, skipping dwc2_hcd_reinit(),
+		 * dwc2_vbus_supply_init() and usb_hcd_resume_root_hub() - the
+		 * root hub was never activated and the host controller's port
+		 * interrupts stayed disabled for good, with nothing in dmesg to
+		 * explain it. Retry for a bounded time instead, matching the
+		 * ~200ms worst-case mode switch measured on this hardware.
+		 */
+		dev_warn(hsotg->dev,
+			 "%s: unexpectedly in device mode (GOTGCTL=%08x GINTSTS=%08x) when activating the root hub - retrying for up to 200ms\n",
+			 __func__, dwc2_readl(hsotg, GOTGCTL),
+			 dwc2_readl(hsotg, GINTSTS));
+
+		timeout = jiffies + msecs_to_jiffies(200);
+		while (dwc2_is_device_mode(hsotg) &&
+		       time_before(jiffies, timeout))
+			usleep_range(1000, 2000);
+
+		spin_lock_irqsave(&hsotg->lock, flags);
+
+		if (dwc2_is_device_mode(hsotg)) {
+			dev_err(hsotg->dev,
+				"%s: still in device mode after 200ms - root hub will NOT be activated (GOTGCTL=%08x GINTSTS=%08x)\n",
+				__func__, dwc2_readl(hsotg, GOTGCTL),
+				dwc2_readl(hsotg, GINTSTS));
+			spin_unlock_irqrestore(&hsotg->lock, flags);
+			return 0;	/* why 0 ?? */
+		}
+
+		dev_info(hsotg->dev,
+			 "%s: recovered host mode after retry, continuing root hub activation\n",
+			 __func__);
 	}
 
 	dwc2_hcd_reinit(hsotg);
--
